    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-slate-300 space-y-6 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">
        1. How Estonia's Corporate Income Tax (CIT) System Functions
      </h2>
      <p>
        Unlike traditional corporate tax systems across Western Europe and North America—which tax corporate net profits at the end of each fiscal calendar year (ranging from 19% in the UK to 25% in Spain or 30% in Germany)—Estonia does not tax corporate profit creation. Under Section 50 of the Estonian Income Tax Act, corporate income tax (CIT) is <strong>deferred indefinitely until profits are distributed as dividends</strong> or deemed profit distributions.
      </p>
      <p>
        When an Estonian private limited company (<em class="text-emerald-300 font-mono">Osaühing</em> or <strong class="text-white">OÜ</strong>) generates €150,000 in software consulting or SaaS revenue, €0 is owed in corporate tax at year-end as long as the funds remain in company accounts, are reinvested into server infrastructure, R&D, product marketing, or invested in yield-generating corporate portfolios.
      </p>

      <!-- Mathematical Breakdown: 0% Deferred Tax vs Standard EU 25% Corporate Tax -->
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">
        2. Mathematical Breakdown: 0% Deferred Tax vs Standard EU 25% Tax
      </h2>
      <p>
        The true power of the Estonian corporate model lies in <strong>pre-tax capital compounding</strong>. Consider a bootstrapped SaaS company generating <strong class="text-white">€100,000 in annual net pre-tax profit</strong>, reinvesting profits at an annual return of <strong class="text-white">10%</strong> over a 5-year and 10-year horizon:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 my-6">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900 border-b border-slate-800 text-[11px] uppercase font-mono text-slate-400">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white">Year</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 font-bold text-rose-400">Standard EU Jurisdiction (25% CIT Annually)</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 font-bold text-emerald-400">Estonian OÜ (0% Deferred CIT Reinvested)</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 font-bold text-cyan-400">Nomad Compounding Delta</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 font-mono text-xs">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Year 1 End</td>
