      <p>
        After 5 years, the Estonian OÜ retains <strong>€152,627 in extra capital</strong> simply because cash was not siphoned off at the end of each tax year. Even if the founder chooses to liquidate the entire portfolio in Year 5 and pay the 20/80 Estonian dividend tax (€610,510 × 20% = €122,102), the founder walks away with <strong>€488,408 net</strong>—exceeding the entire pre-dividend balance of the standard EU company (€457,883).
      </p>

      <!-- Dividend Taxation Math: 20/80 vs 14/86 -->
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">
        3. Dividend Distribution Taxation: 20/80 vs 14/86 Reduced Rate
      </h2>
