        In Estonia, when dividends are distributed, the tax rate is expressed as <strong class="text-white">20/80</strong> of the net dividend payment. For example:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>If an OÜ distributes <strong class="text-white">€80,000 net</strong> to the shareholder, the corporate tax payable to the Estonian Tax and Customs Board (MTA) is <code class="text-emerald-300 font-mono">€80,000 × (20 / 80) = €20,000</code>.</li>
        <li>The total gross distribution is <strong class="text-white">€100,000</strong>, resulting in an effective tax rate of exactly 20% on gross profits.</li>
        <li><strong>Regular Dividends (14/86):</strong> For companies paying regular annual dividends, a reduced CIT rate of 14/86 (effective 14%) applies to distributions up to the average distributed taxable dividend of the previous three calendar years.</li>
      </ul>

